          "<thought>\nI need to combine all 4 subnetworks into a complete resistor network topology. Let me analyze what I have:\n\n1. **Subnet 1**: Connects A to X1 through N1\n   - R1: 2.222\u03a9 (A to N1)\n   - R2: 4.444\u03a9 (N1 to X1)\n\n2. **Subnet 2**: Connects X1 to X2 through N_b1\n   - R1: 5.0\u03a9 (X1 to N_b1)\n   - R2: 40.0\u03a9 (N_b1 to X2)\n   - R3: 20.0\u03a9 (N_b1 to X2) - parallel to R2\n\n3. **Subnet 3**: Connects X2 to X3 through N_c1, N_c2, N_c3\n   - R1: 5.0\u03a9 (X2 to N_c1)\n   - R2: 10.0\u03a9 (N_c1 to N_c2)\n   - R3: 15.0\u03a9 (N_c2 to N_c3)\n   - R4: 20.0\u03a9 (N_c3 to X3)\n\n4. **Subnet 4**: Connects X3 to B through N_d1, N_d2, N_d3\n   - R1: 5\u03a9 (X3 to N_d1)\n   - R2: 10\u03a9 (N_d1 to N_d2)\n   - R3: 15\u03a9 (N_d2 to N_d3)\n   - R4: 20\u03a9 (N_d3 to B)\n\nTo combine these, I need to:\n1. Rename resistors to avoid conflicts (R1-R13)\n2. Merge all connections\n3. Validate against the measurements\n\nLet me create the combined topology with unique resistor names:\n- Subnet 1: R1, R2\n- Subnet 2: R3, R4, R5\n- Subnet 3: R6, R7, R8, R9\n- Subnet 4: R10, R11, R12, R13\n\nTotal: 13 resistors (matches the note)\n</thought>\n\n<action>simulate_circuit_resistance</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"topology\": \"{\\\"resistors\\\": {\\\"R1\\\": 2.222, \\\"R2\\\": 4.444, \\\"R3\\\": 5.0, \\\"R4\\\": 40.0, \\\"R5\\\": 20.0, \\\"R6\\\": 5.0, \\\"R7\\\": 10.0, \\\"R8\\\": 15.0, \\\"R9\\\": 20.0, \\\"R10\\\": 5.0, \\\"R11\\\": 10.0, \\\"R12\\\": 15.0, \\\"R13\\\": 20.0}, \\\"connections\\\": [[\\\"A\\\", \\\"N1\\\", \\\"R1\\\"], [\\\"N1\\\", \\\"X1\\\", \\\"R2\\\"], [\\\"X1\\\", \\\"N_b1\\\", \\\"R3\\\"], [\\\"N_b1\\\", \\\"X2\\\", \\\"R4\\\"], [\\\"N_b1\\\", \\\"X2\\\", \\\"R5\\\"], [\\\"X2\\\", \\\"N_c1\\\", \\\"R6\\\"], [\\\"N_c1\\\", \\\"N_c2\\\", \\\"R7\\\"], [\\\"N_c2\\\", \\\"N_c3\\\", \\\"R8\\\"], [\\\"N_c3\\\", \\\"X3\\\", \\\"R9\\\"], [\\\"X3\\\", \\\"N_d1\\\", \\\"R10\\\"], [\\\"N_d1\\\", \\\"N_d2\\\", \\\"R11\\\"], [\\\"N_d2\\\", 